# Figma Personal Access Token (Alternative Setup)
# This file is a template for token-based Figma MCP setup.
# The primary recommended approach is OAuth (see .context/mcp-setup.md).
# Only use this if OAuth doesn't meet your needs.

# Generate your token at: https://www.figma.com/settings
# Navigate to: Account Settings > Personal Access Tokens > Create new token
# Required scopes: File content (read)
# Copy the token when created (you won't see it again!)

FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_figma_token_here

# Optional: Default Figma file ID for this project
# Extract from URL: https://www.figma.com/file/{FILE_ID}/...
# This can help speed up workflows by having a default file to reference
FIGMA_FILE_ID=

# Optional: Figma team ID
# Extract from URL: https://www.figma.com/files/team/{TEAM_ID}/...
FIGMA_TEAM_ID=

# SECURITY NOTES:
# - Never commit .env.figma to git (it's already in .gitignore)
# - Generate a unique token per team member
# - Rotate tokens regularly for security
# - Use minimum required scopes (File content: read)
# - Revoke tokens immediately if compromised

# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.figma.example .env.figma
# 2. Generate token at https://www.figma.com/settings
# 3. Replace "your_figma_token_here" with your actual token
# 4. Update .mcp.json to use token-based Figma MCP (see .context/mcp-setup.md)
# 5. Restart Claude Code to load environment variables

# TOKEN ROTATION:
# If you need to rotate your token:
# 1. Revoke old token at https://www.figma.com/settings
# 2. Generate new token with same scopes
# 3. Update FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN in this file
# 4. Restart Claude Code
